  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Molecular weight of $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2}=34$ Equivalent weight of $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2}=17$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore 1 \\mathrm{~L}$ of $1 \\mathrm{~N} \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2} \\mathrm{has}=17 \\mathrm{~g}$ of $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore 1$ Lof $1.5 \\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2}$ has $=1.5 \\times 17=25.5 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{of} \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2}$",
    "image": null
